  "decision": "Keep object-per-animal state. The isolated typed-column kernel excludes gather/scatter and is not a production end-to-end win unless typedColumnsEndToEnd repeatedly beats AoS with identical outputs.",
  "limitations": [
    "This isolates one-hour weight/energy transition after feeding; it does not benchmark a full 24-hour engine tick or renderer.",
    "Native Rust measures the same packed numeric kernel and fixture but excludes JSON serialization, FFI and process startup.",
    "Heap snapshots are process-level readings after GC and include engine/test harness memory; they are directional. Typed-buffer bytes are exact. Peak allocation counts are not instrumented; per-snapshot output object counts are known.",
    "Feed intake is calculated once from the deterministic initial scenario state and reused to isolate transition layout."
  ]
